      "explanation": "DISTINCT keyword eliminates rows of query results in SELECT statement and is located before the column name to erase the duplicate. If the DISTINCT keyword is omitted, SQL does not eliminate duplicate and it has the same result when user use ALL  keyword instead of DISTINCT."
